WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:08.010
When Ally arrived at Sandville Print Shop, Mateo was waiting outside for her.

2
00:00:08.011 --> 00:00:11.355
A bell jangled as they entered the shop.

3
00:00:11.356 --> 00:00:19.185
To their surprise, Coach Cross was standing behind the counter, wearing a T-shirt that read Your Message Here.

4
00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:24.698
"Hi, Coach. I thought you said your brother owns this shop," Ally said.

5
00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:31.598
The man laughed. "People always mix up my brother and me!

6
00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:37.749
I'm Eli, Coach Cross' brother. You must be Ally and Mateo.

7
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:44.087
I'll be right with you kids. I just have to make some copies for another customer."

8
00:00:44.088 --> 00:00:47.513
Eli started up one of the shop's large copy machines.

9
00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:52.043
The machine was so loud, Ally could hardly hear her own thoughts.

10
00:00:52.044 --> 00:00:56.929
Eli came back to the counter. "I'm happy to help with your fundraiser.

11
00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:02.325
If you pay for the T-shirts and supply the design, I'll donate the cost of printing the shirts."

12
00:01:02.326 --> 00:01:09.904
"That's very generous of you," Mateo said loudly. "How much are the T-shirts?"

13
00:01:09.905 --> 00:01:13.829
"Five dollars each if you order between twenty and fifty shirts."

14
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:20.034
Eli started to punch numbers into his calculator, but Ally already had the math figured out.

15
00:01:20.035 --> 00:01:28.450
"So, if we print fifty T-shirts, and charge fifteen dollars per shirt, we'll make over seven hundred dollars," she said.

16
00:01:28.451 --> 00:01:34.880
"Minus the $250 you'll have to pay now to buy the T-shirts," Eli reminded her.

17
00:01:34.881 --> 00:01:41.318
"But we don't have $250." Mateo sighed.

18
00:01:41.319 --> 00:01:46.835
Ally pulled out her purse. "Yes, we do! I have a lot of money saved."

19
00:01:46.836 --> 00:01:51.476
"Great, I'll start the paperwork," Eli said.

20
00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:56.501
Mateo pulled Ally aside. "I can't ask you to pay for this, Ally."

21
00:01:56.502 --> 00:02:00.285
"But you're not asking me to pay, Mateo. I'm offering.

22
00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:08.114
Besides, I might as well spend my Earth money now, since it will do me no good once I head back to space with Lainie."

23
00:02:08.115 --> 00:02:11.715
Mateo grinned. "I didn't think of that!

24
00:02:11.716 --> 00:02:16.357
Thanks a lot. It's very nice of you to put the money down for us."

25
00:02:16.358 --> 00:02:23.985
"No problem!"

26
00:02:23.986 --> 00:02:26.403
Ally set the bills on the floor.

27
00:02:26.404 --> 00:02:30.560
Eli and Mateo looked at each other, confused.

28
00:02:30.561 --> 00:02:35.228
"Um, Ally, what are you doing?" Mateo asked.

29
00:02:35.229 --> 00:02:40.479
"You said to put the money down, so I did."

30
00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.132
Eli and Mateo laughed.

31
00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:47.552
"What's so funny?" Ally asked.

32
00:02:47.553 --> 00:02:54.258
"Putting money down is just an expression," Mateo said. "It means to pay for something."

33
00:02:54.259 --> 00:03:01.519
"Oh! I get it." Ally laughed as she picked the money up and handed it to Eli.

34
00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:05.355
"Great," he said. "Send me your design as soon as you can.

35
00:03:05.356 --> 00:03:08.677
I need only a day or two to print the shirts."

36
00:03:08.678 --> 00:03:14.867
"Thanks so much, Eli!" Mateo and Ally turned to leave when a dark-haired woman entered the shop.

37
00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:17.709
Her arms were full of blueprints.

38
00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:23.552
"Hello, Mateo," the woman said. "It's so nice to see you."

39
00:03:23.553 --> 00:03:28.441
"Hello, Mayor Clark," Mateo said.

40
00:03:28.442 --> 00:03:31.943
"You must be Ally," the mayor said.

41
00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:37.772
"I've eaten at Ray's Diner many times, but you're always so busy, I've never had the chance to meet you.

42
00:03:37.773 --> 00:03:41.077
I just love all you've done for the diner."

43
00:03:41.078 --> 00:03:44.672
"That's very nice of you to say," Ally said.

44
00:03:44.673 --> 00:03:51.456
"That Gourmet Greta review brought a lot of positive attention to the town, and so many new tourists.

45
00:03:51.457 --> 00:03:57.775
And now Lainie Polk's launch is set to bring even more people here!

46
00:03:57.776 --> 00:04:03.409
In many ways, the plans in these blueprints are happening thanks to you, Ally."

47
00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.268
Ally grinned proudly.

48
00:04:05.269 --> 00:04:09.234
"Just wait until my parents hear about this," she thought.

49
00:04:09.235 --> 00:04:15.699
"They will be so impressed to hear that even the mayor was thankful for all I did on Earth!"

50
00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:20.003
"Madam Mayor, what are the plans for?" Mateo asked.

51
00:04:20.004 --> 00:04:28.807
Just then his phone rang. "Oh, excuse me for a moment, this is my friend Bethany on the phone."

52
00:04:28.808 --> 00:04:37.313
"Of course." Mayor Clark set her blueprints on the counter and started talking to Eli about making copies of them.

53
00:04:37.314 --> 00:04:43.216
Between Mateo's talking on the phone and the noise of the copy machines, Ally wasn't sure she heard right.

54
00:04:43.217 --> 00:04:47.305
But she thought she heard the mayor say "soccer field."

55
00:04:47.306 --> 00:04:52.191
She tried to read the mayor's mind, but the shop was still too noisy.

56
00:04:52.192 --> 00:04:55.232
"I must have misheard her," Ally thought.

57
00:04:55.233 --> 00:05:01.091
"Why would an important person like the mayor of Sandville be thinking about a kids' soccer field?"

58
00:05:01.092 --> 00:05:07.743
Mateo disconnected his call. "Hey, Ally, Bethany and Kate want us to meet them at the park.

59
00:05:07.744 --> 00:05:11.859
They have a design for the T-shirt, and a big surprise!"

60
00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:23.110
"Sounds great!" Ally said. "Let's go!"

